  "analyzer_note": "The three r3a runs packaged a native_stream.py with a rename hook; the committed analyzers apply the same context signal_aliases mapping in their own samples() reader so the frozen native_stream.py of the B cases stays byte-identical.",
  "post_layout_scope": "Extracted SAR macro and extracted CDAC; reference word with cell LPE; comparator and bootstrap schematic; ideal top-level wiring and supplies.",
  "findings": [
    "SS cold frame 0 fails the control check: at t=0 the DC solution leaves the comparator latch balanced with its clock high (COMP_P/COMP_N 0.42/0.70 V with 256 mV input, unchanged for 60 ns), so CMP_CLK is still high for 0.2 ns after the first tracking opening. This is a non-physical initial state; frame 0 reads its code and frame 1 with the same input passes.",
    "The same overlap occurs in operation when a sample aborts a comparison: 71-72 ps in the pre-layout FF-cold restart runs, none at TT. The restart analyzer does not check a clock that is already high.",
    "The SAR macro was extracted at the typical interconnect corner, while the SS and FF pre-layout runs used CWORST_T and CBEST_T cell LPE; the SS and FF post-layout margins are therefore not worst-case."
  ],
  "open_items": [
    "Re-extract the macro at CWORST_T and CBEST_T and rerun SS and FF cold",
    "Treat frame 0 as warm-up and report the clock/tracking overlap as a measured diagnostic",
    "Top-level placement, routing, fill and terminal-voltage scan"
  ]
}
